Enhancement: Apps can skip the version of the next write to a file

Editors that save a document automatically while it is open, such as
Collabora Online in the office app oco_office, created a new version of the
file with every automatic save. With the new method
OCA\Files_Versions\Storage::skipNextVersion($path) an app tells the versions
app that the next write to the given path creates no version. This applies
once and only within the current request: the following write creates a
version as before, so a save requested by the user still does. The path is
the one in the file tree of the user, as the filesystem hooks pass it, for
example /Documents/Report.odt. Writes without this call are not affected.
